# ICM workspace and voice profile.
# This repository is PUBLIC and is Monica's deploy repo. The workspace holds
# candid working material about her job search: target employers, an
# assessment of her weaknesses, salary positioning, research outputs. None of
# that belongs on a public URL under her own name.
# It lives in the private mirror instead: github.com/tomas-fw/monica-portfolio
CONTEXT.md
stages/
setup/
.ghost/
ghost-drafts/
_shared/product/

# local asset-prep scratch (not part of the site)
/tmp/

# local asset-prep scratch (not part of the site)
/tmp/

# Raw source material: 129MB of Drive exports, client files and her CV.
# This repository is PUBLIC. These are the originals the plates are cut from,
# they are not served, and several are client work that is not ours to publish.
# The rule exists on the cinematic-universe branch; main never had it, so any
# branch cut from main is one `git add .` away from committing all of it.
/produccion/

# ...but the scripts that cut the plates ARE tracked. They are code, they carry
# the provenance for every crop, and a pipeline nobody can read is a pipeline
# nobody can check. Only their 129MB of inputs stay out.
!/produccion/
/produccion/*
!/produccion/*.py
!/produccion/blender/
/produccion/blender/*
!/produccion/blender/*.py
